    "provenance": "Base colour re-baked (Cycles CPU, emission, selected-to-active) from the approved TRELLIS source mesh; there is no rear-view projection, so the back, far side and underside are as TRELLIS invented them from the single approved concept. Tangent normals baked from the source geometry and whiteout-blended with colour relief; AO baked from the decimated geometry; roughness set inside declared regions (the dark nose and eyes by colour value at the head, hooves by height) and otherwise the default, both reduced by colour detail; no metal and no dye mask (the deer is never dyed). Base colour lifted by luma power toneGamma (chroma ratios kept), set by eye in review renders, not calibrated against the concept. Artistic derivation, not measured PBR."
  },
  "textureNote": "Baked at 1024 and stored at 512 px, as the sheep, to keep the version 3 world's texture memory within its 160 MiB budget; a deer is at most about 150 px tall at the closest camera."
